cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper listed under preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "PLUME: unsteady, polydisperse Bayesian inversion of deep-sea tephra deposits"
abstract: >-
  Python package and analysis scripts that invert the sieve fractions of a
  deep-sea tephra deposit for the mass-weighted distribution of umbrella volume
  flux, convert it to a heat flux, measure how many source modes the deposit
  resolves, and compare candidate heat sources for megaplumes by Bayesian
  evidence. Applied to the NESCA push cores of Clague, Paduan and Davis (2009).
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bijanf/PLUME"
keywords:
  - megaplume
  - hydrothermal plume
  - tephra
  - Bayesian inversion
  - submarine eruption
